{"name":"Give Me Your Love","hex":"#ee88ff","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"give","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move, shift, provide something abstract or concrete to someone or something or somewhere.","To make a present or gift of."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The amount of bending that something undergoes when a force is applied to it; a tendency to yield under pressure; resilience."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give"},{"term":"your","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["Belonging to you; of you; related to you (singular; one owner).","Belonging to you; of you; related to you (plural; more owners)."]},{"part":"Contraction","definitions":["Misspelling of you're."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/your"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Give Me Your Love (Barbara Mason album)","blocks":[{"text":"Give Me Your Love is a 1973 album by Barbara Mason. Buddha Records' decision to record an album was due to the success of Mason's version of the Curtis Mayfield title song. The album included mature subject matter such as \"Bed and Board\", and \"You Can Be With the One You Don't Love\", expressing the desire for a lover outside of marriage. She was the first soul singer to record in the heavy breathing disco style later adopted by Donna Summer among others."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Give_Me_Your_Love_%28Barbara_Mason_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Give_Me_Your_Love_(Barbara_Mason_album)"},{"title":"Give Me Your Love (Sylvia Striplin album)","blocks":[{"text":"Give Me Your Love is the 1981 debut and only released album of singer Sylvia Striplin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Give_Me_Your_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Give_Me_Your_Love_(Sylvia_Striplin_album)"},{"title":"Give Me Your Love (Sigala song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Give Me Your Love\" is the fourth single produced by British DJ and record producer Sigala. It features the vocals from British singer John Newman and partial production work from American electric guitarist Nile Rodgers and was released on 29 April 2016 by Ministry of Sound."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Give-Me-Your-Love-by-Sigala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Give_Me_Your_Love_(Sigala_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/58/Give_Me_Your_Love_%28Barbara_Mason_album%29.jpg/250px-Give_Me_Your_Love_%28Barbara_Mason_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Give_Me_Your_Love_%28Barbara_Mason_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/58/Give_Me_Your_Love_%28Barbara_Mason_album%29.jpg/250px-Give_Me_Your_Love_%28Barbara_Mason_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGive_Me_Your_Love_(Barbara_Mason_album).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ca/Give_Me_Your_Love.jpg/250px-Give_Me_Your_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Give_Me_Your_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","sr